Node ID=500 divine spirit explanation elemental
Text=Divine spirits have opposed the Daevas since humankind first knew good from evil. Humans have given them many names throughout time. The Persians knew us as the immortal amesha spentas. In Africa, we are known as the ombwiri, while Christendom sometimes calls us cherubim, and in the east we are the holy kurabi. Each divine spirit represents a virtue and possesses a power of some good aspect.
